WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.960
There are various properties of images formed
by spherical mirrors… the

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.560
position, the size, and the nature of the
image. These properties vary as the

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.750
object’s distance from the mirror varies.
The property that we are going to

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:23.410
discuss in detail in this video is the SIZE
of the image.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.619
For a concave mirror, there are three possibilities
for the size of the image

00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:33.320
relative to the object! Basically, the image
can be enlarged, the image can be

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.430
of the same size or can also be diminished
or smaller in size.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.960
For a convex mirror, the image is always smaller
in size unless the object

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.690
touches the mirror! In that case, the image
will be of the same size as the

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.240
object.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.610
Now if we were to compare the size of the
image with the size of the object,

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:58.391
then we will take their ratios. That is, the
ratio of size of the image to the size

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:04.720
of the object. And this ratio is what we call
MAGNIFICATION. It is denoted by

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:11.580
‘m’. Let’s move to a new page!
In our ray diagram, the sizes of the object

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:16.660
and the image are nothing but the
heights of the object and image. So ‘m’

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.860
will be equal to ‘h i over h o’. Let’s
do a

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:25.060
bit of math now. Suppose the height of the
image is greater than the height of

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:32.690
the object. This means that image is enlarged.
Now answer this question. If the term in the

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:37.030
numerator is greater than the
term in the denominator, then the ratio will

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:44.850
be?
Yes, their ratio will be greater than one.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:51.080
What if ‘h i is less than h o’? Yes, the
ratio will be less than one. The image is

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:56.240
DIMINISHED.
What if they are equal? Their equality implies

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:02.590
that both the object and image
are of SAME size. The ratio will be one!

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:07.630
If you notice that in all the three cases
we are assuming something. We are

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:14.110
assuming both h o and h i to be non-zero.
But can they be zero?

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:18.629
We know that when the object is at infinity,
its point sized image is formed at

00:02:18.629 --> 00:02:24.459
the focal point. So here we can take size
of the image as zero. However

00:02:24.459 --> 00:02:30.889
theoretically we say that when the object
is at infinity, the image is point sized.

00:02:30.889 --> 00:02:36.669
But in reality, this is not a point sized
image, because we cannot define infinity.

00:02:36.669 --> 00:02:42.609
The image, however small it is, still has
some dimensions. So in reality, h i

00:02:42.609 --> 00:02:48.049
cannot be zero. It can be a really small number,
for example, zero point zero

00:02:48.049 --> 00:02:53.260
zero zero zero zero five but never zero. We
can apply the same logic for the

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:59.459
object size. So h i and h o cannot be zero
in reality.

00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:04.139
Now there is a relation between the magnification
and the object distance ‘u’

00:03:04.139 --> 00:03:09.739
and image distance ‘v’. the relation is
that ‘h i’ over ‘h o’ is equal to

00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:11.859
negative
v over u.

00:03:11.859 --> 00:03:16.730
This relation is very easy to prove. I will
give you rough sketch of its proof in

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:21.459
another video in this playlist, but first
let us solve a few problems based on

00:03:21.459 --> 00:03:22.459
magnification.
Here’s the first problem!

00:03:22.459 --> 00:03:23.459
A side-view convex mirror of an automobile
has its radius of curvature as 3m. If

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:24.459
a bus is located 5m away from this mirror,
then find the

00:03:24.459 --> 00:03:27.990
a. position of the image
b. nature of the image

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:28.990
c. ratio of the ‘size of the image’ to
the ‘size of the object’

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:32.540
We will see the solution in the next part
of the video!

